{"name":"Nursery Wall","hex":"#9ebcb7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"nursery","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where nursing (“breastfeeding”) or the raising of children is carried on.\n Especially in European countries: a room or area in a household set apart for the care of children.\n\n An institution for small children who not yet have begun primary school during daytime (when their parents work); a daycare centre.","Especially in European countries: a room or area in a household set apart for the care of children."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/nursery"},{"term":"wall","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A rampart of earth, stones etc. built up for defensive purposes.","A structure built for defense surrounding a city, castle etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enclose with, or as if with, a wall or walls.","To use a wallhack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wall"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nursery (room)","blocks":[{"text":"A nursery is a bedroom within a house or other dwelling set aside for an infant or toddler."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Baby_nursery_room.jpg/330px-Baby_nursery_room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nursery_(room)","wikidata":"Q1741939"},{"title":"Wall","blocks":[{"text":"A wall is a structure and a surface that defines an area; carries a load; provides security, shelter, or soundproofing; or serves a decorative purpose. There are various types of walls, including border barriers between countries, brick walls, defensive walls in fortifications, and retaining walls that hold back dirt, stone, water, or noise. Walls can also be found in buildings, where they support roofs, floors, and ceilings, enclose spaces, and provide shelter and security."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Noel_2005_P%C3%A9